id: pm-web-y80b
title: i18n plumbing + German locale for package-owned UI strings
description: Add i18n plumbing (locale catalogs + t() helper + locale resolution + language selector) and a complete German (de) locale for all package-owned UI strings in the pm-web SPA. Part of epic pm-cli-website-m1ut (German localization).
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-17T06:03:26.795Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-27T23:17:21.635Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-27T23:04:16.626Z"
author: pi-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Flat JSON catalogs (en.json + de.json) cover all package-owned UI strings: auth screen, nav, banners, settings incl. registration acknowledgement, consent UI; Tiny typed t(key, params?) helper with en fallback; locale resolution localStorage.pmLocale -> navigator.language prefix match -> en; Language selector (en/Deutsch) in settings view persists choice and sets document.documentElement.lang dynamically; Dates use active locale (de-DE when de) instead of hard-coded en-US; Server API error strings stay English on the wire; translate at display layer mapping known errors to catalog keys (fallback: raw message); Legal-page localization documented as overlay-owned (operator concern); German disclaimer string present; selector does not promise translated legal pages; German translations complete and natural (Sie-Form); no visible English when de active for package-owned strings; Unit tests: locale resolution order, t() fallback + params, catalog parity (every de key exists for every en key); Functional check: auth screen renders German when localStorage.pmLocale=de"
release: 2026.7.17-1
resolution: Work completed and released in 2026.7.18. Release attribution set explicitly so pm-changelog --respect-item-release files the entry under 2026.7.18 instead of the current release notes.
expected_result: "A closed item whose changelog entry appears under the 2026.7.18 heading it actually shipped in, leaving the current release notes untouched."
actual_result: "Before this closeout the item had remained in_progress with no activity since its work shipped, so the delivery was missing from the changelog while still being counted as open work in every fleet audit. Closing it with an explicit release attribution is what added the historical entry."
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-17T06:12:19.310Z",pi-agent,"Implementation summary (i18n plumbing + German locale for package-owned UI strings):\n\n- Added public/src/i18n/ with en.json + de.json flat dotted-key catalogs covering all package-owned UI strings (auth screen, nav, banners, cookie-consent banner, settings incl. registration acknowledgement + language selector) plus API/OIDC error messages (mapped at the display layer) and a German legal-adjacent disclaimer string.\n- Added public/src/i18n.ts: typed t(key, params?) helper with en fallback, locale resolution (localStorage.pmLocale -> navigator.language prefix match -> en), async catalog loading via fetch, DOM binding via data-i18n/data-i18n-html/data-i18n-title/data-i18n-placeholder/data-i18n-aria attributes, document.documentElement.lang sync, translateError() display-layer mapping (fallback: raw message), and localeDate() (de-DE when de) replacing hard-coded en-US.\n- index.html: added data-i18n wiring to the auth screen, nav/top-bar, offline/install banners, and cookie-consent banner; added an inline head script to set <html lang> from localStorage.pmLocale before first paint.\n- auth.ts + settings.ts: replaced hard-coded English strings with t() calls; settings now uses localeDate() for the account-created date and exposes an en/Deutsch language selector that persists the choice and re-applies translations; API errors flow through translateError().\n- sw.ts: added /src/i18n.js, /src/i18n/en.json, /src/i18n/de.json to the service-worker precache list.\n- src/app.ts: documented that legal-page localization is overlay-owned (operator concern via PM_WEB_LEGAL_DIR) — the standalone legal HTML does not load the SPA bundle so the SPA t()/catalog plumbing cannot reach it; the language selector deliberately does not promise translated legal pages (see settings.languageHint), and a German disclaimer string (legal.disclaimer) is provided for translated legal-adjacent UI.\n\nTests added (test/i18n.test.ts): catalog parity (every en key exists in de, non-empty; no extra de keys; de differs from en for non-structural strings), locale resolution order (storage -> navigator prefix -> en; null skips a source), t()/translate fallback + {param} substitution, error.* English-value uniqueness for an unambiguous reverse map, translateError unknown-message passthrough, and a functional check simulating applyTranslations on the auth-screen block with the de catalog asserting no English auth strings remain.\n\nQuality gates: npm run typecheck, npm run build, npm test (100 passing incl. new i18n tests), npm run audit:prod, npm run pack:dry-run, and npm run changelog:check all green. German uses Sie-Form throughout."
  "2026-07-17T06:27:18.107Z",pi-agent,"CodeRabbit review fixes (PR #43, branch feat/i18n-de-locale) — all 5 findings addressed, no suppressions:\n\n1. **index.html first-paint hint (navigator.language negotiation):** The inline head script now falls back to the browser language when no valid `pmLocale` is stored, mirroring `resolveLocale()` by recognizing German-prefixed `navigator.language` values (e.g. `de-DE`) as `de`. A first visit with a German browser no longer flashes `lang=\"en\"`. Persisted de/en preference precedence and existing error handling are preserved.\n\n2. **index.html accessible names (a11y):** Added `data-i18n-aria=\"nav.theme.title\"` to the theme toggle and `data-i18n-aria=\"nav.settings\"` to the settings button so their `aria-label` values update with the selected language for German screen-reader users (reusing existing translation keys).\n\n3. **i18n.ts resilient localStorage:** Wrapped ALL localStorage access in try/catch — resolving the storage reference (`safeLocalStorage`), `getItem()` in `resolveLocale`, and `setItem()` in `setLocale`. A `SecurityError` (privacy/incognito mode) is now swallowed and startup continues with the existing locale fallback instead of rejecting `initI18n()`/`setLocale()` and preventing rendering.\n\n4. **i18n.ts stale-fetch guard:** Added a monotonically increasing `localeReqId`; each `setLocale` invocation records its id and, after every awaited catalog fetch, verifies it is still the latest before committing any state (`enCatalog`, `activeCatalog`, `initialized`, `syncHtmlLang`, `applyTranslations`). The fetched catalog is captured in a local before the guard check, so a slow earlier German fetch finishing after a newer `en` selection is discarded and can never overwrite the active catalog. Stale requests return without applying.\n\n5. **settings.ts localized confirmDialog buttons:** Extended the shared `confirmDialog()` API with an optional `labels?: { cancel?, confirm? }` parameter (defaults preserve the existing English \"Cancel\"/\"Delete\"/\"Confirm\" behavior, so other callers are unaffected). The GitHub token-clear flow now passes `t('dialog.cancel')` / `t('dialog.confirm')` via new catalog keys `dialog.cancel` / `dialog.confirm` / `dialog.delete` (en + de) so the German token-clear dialog is fully localized.\n\nTests added/extended (test/i18n.test.ts): first-paint hint navigator negotiation (runs the inline script against fakes), throwing `storage.getItem` fallback, throwing `safeLocalStorage` getter no-abort, throwing `storage.setItem` no-abort on `setLocale`, stale catalog fetch discarded when a newer `setLocale` wins, and `dialog.*` catalog-key parity/localization. Catalog parity + \"every wired data-i18n key has a de translation\" checks still green (covers the new `data-i18n-aria` bindings and `dialog.*` keys).\n\nQuality gates: `npm run typecheck`, `npm run build`, `npm test` (106 passing, +6 i18n), `npm run changelog:check` — all green. German uses Sie-Form throughout."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T23:17:10.266Z",claude-code,"Release attribution corrected to 2026.7.17-1 after review. The first attribution used the item's last-activity DATE, which is unsound: an item can be touched before the release that finally carried its code. Verified instead by tag containment — git tag --contains 92175e2 reports 2026.7.17-1 as the first release holding the implementation commit. Greptile caught this on PR #67 by noticing a historical release predating its implementation."
close_reason: "Retired as shipped: the i18n plumbing and German locale, shipped as public/src/i18n/de.json was completed and released in 2026.7.18, but the item was never closed and sat in progress ever since, inflating every fleet audit."
body: ""
